From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephen Bates <sbates@raithlin.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 21:33:02 -0500
Subject: [RFC PATCH 4/8] ionic: track Rx buffers as netmem

Keep a netmem_ref instead of a struct page pointer for each Rx buffer,
and use the netmem variants of the page pool and skb helpers:
page_pool_alloc_netmem(), page_pool_get_dma_addr_netmem(),
page_pool_put_full_netmem(), page_pool_dma_sync_netmem_for_cpu(),
skb_add_rx_frag_netmem() and skb_frag_fill_netmem_desc().

The places that need the page or its address say so by going through
ionic_rx_buf_page() and ionic_rx_buf_va(): the copybreak copy, and XDP,
which reads the first buffer and hands pages to the Tx path. They only
ever see pages.

No functional change: nothing gives the page pool a memory provider
yet, so every netmem is still a page, and
page_pool_dma_sync_netmem_for_cpu() only differs from
page_pool_dma_sync_for_cpu() for a pool whose memory provider turned
the sync off.
